    rdf:value """They could not answer, and so, man-wise, they sat on me and said it was a foolish question.I also asked why it was that “ideated movement” in painting is always agreeable while ideated movement in music can sometimes be hideously disagreeable. Is it that what we find disagreeable is only  motion , not movement – that is to say, suggested motion of parts of the body – while the agreeable ideated movements of good music are general movements of the whole body, such as suggest flying, swimming, etc.?
We lunched with Placci and then called on the Buttles. Bernhard thereupon went to Alinari’s, and I called on Janet whom I found ill and depressed, and on Maud whom I found still more rampantly moral, and on Mrs. Lovett whom I found busy bathing her baby. 
Herbert Horne came to dinner, and """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 17 ;
